  "placement": "Book page 219, topic 8.3.1 প্রতিবিম্ব: next to চিত্র ৮.০৮–৮.১০ (pages 218–220: rays from X reflected by mirror AB seem to come from X′; XP = X′P; the image X′Y′ of XY); the last step also serves the উদাহরণ on page 221 (চিত্র ৮.১২, a mirror half your height).",
  "order": 1,
  "maintainers": ["RadeenXALNW"],
  "units": "m",
  "description": "Interactive 3D figure for the image in a plane mirror, book page 219, topic 8.3.1, next to চিত্র ৮.০৮–৮.১০, and the উদাহরণ on page 221 (চিত্র ৮.১২). A realistic boy of 1.5 m stands before a silvered-glass mirror on a plain floor under a sky-to-blush backdrop; his faded image, the mirror's exact reflection of him, stands as far behind it. The student drags the boy and XP = X′P stays true, and measures that XY and X′Y′ are equal; draws the rays from his head and his feet to his eye, with θi = θr read back from the reflected vectors, and extends them behind the mirror to X′ and Y′, where no real light goes (অবাস্তব প্রতিবিম্ব); then drags the mirror's edges, watching what he really sees in a small picture from his eye, until head and feet both show: half his height, 0.75 m, at 1 m or at 10 m. Five test questions. Offline, Bangla and English.",
  "tags": [
    "light",
    "reflection",
    "plane-mirror",
    "image",
    "virtual-image",
    "full-length-mirror",
    "law-of-reflection",
    "bangla"
  ],
